A2  the AM-fair pairing quadruple Q_b = {s_o, s_e = s_o + b, t_o = T_b(s_o), t_e = s_e/2}
    (b = +1: pairs {2i-1, 2i}; b = -1: pairs {2i, 2i+1}; THM-4470 section 1)
  |s_o| <= 2001, both sheets: 4000 non-degenerate quadruples; degenerate exactly at |s_o| = 1
  (b=+1: {1,2} the 2-cycle, {-1,0} two fixed points; b=-1: {0,1} fixed points, {-2,-1} the 2-cycle)
  sheet -1, neg side: increasing order to < se < so < te
  sheet -1, pos side: increasing order te < se < so < to
  sheet +1, neg side: increasing order to < so < se < te
  sheet +1, pos side: increasing order te < so < se < to
  Theorem A (checked on every quadruple above):
   (a) map arcs + order (asc or desc): C3+SNK iff b*s_o >= 3 (T_b reverses the pair), TT iff b*s_o <= -3
   (b) inverse-tree arcs (t_e -D-> s_e, t_o -E-> s_o) + order: SRC+C3 iff b*s_o >= 3, TT otherwise
   (c) rho(x) = (s_o+s_e) - x swaps s_o<->s_e, t_o<->t_e (AM-fairness), reverses order, fixes the map-arc
       set: rho: (M,O) ~ (M,O^op) and rho: (F+)^op ~ F-.  So TIME REVERSAL = CONVERSE up to rho.
   (d) nu(x) = -x carries Q_b(s_o) onto Q_-b(-s_o) with the same labels and the reversed order:
       F+(nu Q) = F+_desc(Q) ~ F+(Q) (same class): NEGATION FIXES THE CLASS.
   (e) EXACT labelled identity: (F+(Q))^op = F-(nu Q), i.e. converse = negation o time-reversal.
   (f) H(F+) = 2 + sgn(b s_o): on positive pairs H = 3 on the 3n+1 sheet, H = 1 on the 3n-1 sheet.
   (g) (s_o - s_e)(T(s_o) - T(s_e)) = -b s_o: the pair is order-reversed by T_b iff b s_o > 0.
