B0  a fixed vertex set V: map arcs {x, T_b(x)} inside V + ascending order on the other pairs
  3000 random vertex sets V c [3, ~90]: the tournaments of T_+ and T_- coincide on every V.
  Reason (PROVED): on positive x every odd step goes up and every even step halves, so each map
  arc agrees with the order except the halving arcs {x, x/2}, which are the same on both sheets.
  => a map+order tournament can see the sheet only through the choice of the vertex set.
