C0  Redei's theorem as the fixed-point count of an involution (OCF / Grinberg-Stanley form)
  1147 tournaments (all with n <= 5, random n = 6, 7): H = #X, X = {(sigma, bits)}; the involution
  flipping the bit of the cycle through the least moved point is fixed-point-free except at (id, ()).
  So H = 1 (mod 2): Redei = 'the identity is the only permutation without a nontrivial cycle'.
  (Higher digits: H = sum_{k<m} alpha_k 2^k mod 2^m, THM-466; checked on windows in part B.)
